# License scope

The owner selected the following licenses on 2026-10-26:

- Tools, tests, build/CI configuration, and their technical documentation: **MIT**, see `LICENSES/MIT.txt`.
- New English location descriptions, Simplified Chinese translations and any project-owned editorial contributions to them: **CC BY-SA 4.0**, see `LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt` and `https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/`.

The latter scope covers the description fields in `data/descriptions/*.jsonl` and the resulting `*_desc` values in the built localization files. Credit the **EU5 Location Descriptions contributors**, retain the per-location Wikipedia credits and revision/history links in `sources/`, identify modifications, and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or a compatible license where required. The descriptions are AI-assisted summaries and translations, modified from consulted source material; they are not verbatim Wikipedia pages. The official EU5 description that opens each of the 257 `extends_official` entries is Paradox's text, kept unchanged and not relicensed; the license covers only the paragraphs after it. Upstream copyright notices and exceptions remain applicable.

The licenses grant only rights that the project contributors have authority to grant. Facts and interoperability identifiers are not claimed as exclusively owned. Paradox game files, trademarks, third-party texts and third-party artwork are not relicensed. AI-generated promotional artwork is separately described in `workshop/assets/README.md` and is not included in the above MIT/text license scopes. See `CREDITS.md` and `NOTICE.md`.
